### Mathematics

Flat-space massless scalar wave on Minkowski background, spherically symmetric ansatz φ(t,r). Wave equation: -∂_t²φ + ∇²φ = 0 → ∂_t²φ = ∂_r²φ + (2/r)∂_rφ.

Define ψ = r φ → ∂_t²ψ = ∂_r²ψ for r>0, with regularity ψ(0,t)=0.

Exact solutions used:
1. Standing mode: ψ_k(r,t) = sin(k r) cos(k t), φ = sin(kr)cos(kt)/r.
2. Outgoing pulse (method of images): ψ(r,t) = F(r - t) - F(-r - t), F(s) = exp(-(s-r0)²/(2σ²)). For σ=1.5, r0=10.
